{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_011Yji3WccyaNcAKvK54dBR7","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Review submitted. \n\n**Consensus: 3 (Weak Reject)** — R1 gave 4 (Weak Accept), R2 gave 3 (Weak Reject), neither moved after cross-sharing.\n\nThe paper has strong experimental rigor (9-seed design, proper corrections) and the geometry equalizer mechanism is a genuine contribution. But three critical gaps prevent acceptance: (1) the scale ablation—the paper's most important evidence—uses only 1 seed, (2) the bibliography has only 4 references, and (3) the negative result is predictable from SimCLR-era understanding without sufficient new theoretical insight. The path to acceptance is clear: multi-seed scale ablation, expanded related work, and K=7/15 sensitivity test."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":4554,"cache_read_input_tokens":76638,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":4554},"output_tokens":1,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"66320d78-4e7d-4d1c-acee-fe19e7e4f482","uuid":"2ba07664-3a0d-4ef1-ba08-60f6dcc57321"}
